WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back, Natasha.
-Thanks, Seth.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.936 line:92%
-Congratulations on the show.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really something special.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.640
-For those who haven't seen it,
the premise is --

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are a woman,
on her 36th birthday,

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:15.448
who keeps dying and then going
back and reliving that birthday.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.182 size:75% position:38% line:92%
over and over again.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:22.288
-Yeah. It's essentially sort of
an existential adventure show,

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
involving multiple loops
and deaths.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:28.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's hilarious.
You're going to love it.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.362 line:92%
You're really going to enjoy it.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.197 line:92%
-But it has been a show that --

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone I know has seen it,
we like talking about it.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
We like trying to
deconstruct it.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.938
Are you surprised that you made
an existential adventure show,

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.441
as you said, and people
have been so drawn to it?

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I mean, I am.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.144
And, in the first place, I would
say I'm also --

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:44.878 line:92%
You know, I'm blown away.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so, you know,
definitively personal to me

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:53.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I am very moved that
it's connecting on this level.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yes, I definitely think
it's indicative of

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:00.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
the troubling times we're in
that it's connected

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
for so many
other people, as well.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:07.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's essentially a show
that's saying,

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, we're all broken
on the inside.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.171 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Let's do it together."

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is
a really lovely message.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.576
And I should say, because this
is eight episodes on Netflix

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.711 size:84% position:42%
and the highest praise
I can have for it is --

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.580 line:92%
it starts great and ends better.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I feel like there are
shows where people say,

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You've got to give it
five episodes."

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to say,
"I have a life."

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.254 line:92%
Whereas this starts great,

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.490
and then you can say to people,
"Oh, stick around,

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they know
exactly where they're going."

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.294 line:92%
And because this isn't just this

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.163
very personal autobiographical
show that you helped create,

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.966
there is also -- There is,
like, a science-fiction element

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:43.670
and a plotting element that
you guys took very seriously.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.639
This is like "A Beautiful Mind."
There you go.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.207 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There you go.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is fully
from the writers's room

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
of getting all
the time lines straight.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is actually
Michael Bricker,

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
the wonderful
production designer,

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.781 line:92%
who had a hell of a time,

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
because what he was
doing here is --

00:01:56.583 --> 00:02:00.386 size:84% position:42%
you know, he's managing
loops and time lines

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.154 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and multiple deaths.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our poor script supervisor,
Melissa Yap.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, she came from
"Orange is the New Black."

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's amazing.
And this was an endless game.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.596 line:92%
It was almost like, you know,

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.232 size:81% position:41%
Jodie Foster searching
for Hannibal Lecter,

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.166 line:92%
only she didn't even know that

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
she was looking for
Hannibal at the time.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:19.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's a real, you know,
cross-sectioning scenario.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, yet, you drew from,
you know,

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:24.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
this very personal place
and you drew from your life.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:28.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've known you for a long
time, and I've always --

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:29.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
we know each other well.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Then you know I'm a big fan
of Viktor Frankl's

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:34.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Man's Search for Meaning,"
so -- Yes.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I've always felt --
And I feel like

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe other people
feel this way, too.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always felt like I knew you
better than I did,

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.662
because I feel as though
you're a very open person

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I feel like maybe
that's one of the things

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
people are responding to
in this show is --

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:48.501
they can tell,
"Oh, I've seen Natasha in things

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the years
and I've liked her,

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
but this is
the purest version of her

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.872 line:92%
I've ever seen of her onscreen."

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean,
I think that that's --

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:57.343
You know, just speaking frankly,
because I do know you,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that's the,
sort of, like, heavy part

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
to take in, you know,
as somebody who has been

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:04.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
working in this thing
for a long time.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:07.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I started show biz
back before

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
anybody here was born,
including me.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:17.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it's just so,
you know, heavy and deep that,

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:22.235
you know, something so personal
is connecting in this way.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.470
But, yeah, you know, I mean,
it's a lot of connective tissue.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.607
We had such an incredible room,
and there's so many creators.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:31.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your friend Amy Poehler,
of course, co-created the show

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:31.778 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and Leslye Headland.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:35.815
And we had all female writers
and directors on the show.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I think it was really --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.420 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:44.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I do think it was also
sort of, kind of like

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
a testament to what happens
if you just, you know,

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:51.297
try to avoid small talk, like I
do desperately, in this life

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.899 line:92%
and sort of aim to kind of

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.934 size:75% position:38%
tell your version of
the truth, you know?

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You now -- I know how
you feel about small talk.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:00.773
I would assume, because you made
this very personal show,

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:04.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
people feel a comfort
to come up and talk to you.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.713
And now they probably want to
talk to you about this show,

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.447 size:84% position:42% line:92%
which is great for you,

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that's not
small talk anymore.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:11.751 size:81% position:41%
-And, yet, you know,
the great relief is --

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I'm sort of like
a Paul Giamatti type.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What does that mean?
-You know what it means.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.924 size:81% position:41%
It's like, you know,
you see Paul Giamatti,

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.525
you're thrilled, but you're not
going to go up to him

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.328
and be, like, "Hey,
'American Splendor' was great."

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:22.996 line:92%
I mean, where does it go?

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:25.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like we all know --
But it's kind of like

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:26.966 size:75% position:38% line:92%
a New York character

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:30.637
that's more like a garden gnome
or a leprechaun.

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:32.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
A twin. A twin even.
-I see.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.340 line:92%
-I'm happy to kind of see you.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I may be projecting
an air of like,

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, buddy,
I might follow you home,

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.748 line:92%
so why don't you --" Right?

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not even doing it
on purpose.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just might
follow you home, you know?

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I think there is
something true

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:50.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the quintessential
New York celebrity

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:53.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
that because they're
so New York and the fact

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they have stayed there
for their career,

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.429 size:88% position:44% line:92%
they're -- They don't --

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.631 line:92%
-You begin is what it is, Seth.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
You begin to blend into
the pavement.

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like a series of ash
piles on the street.

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:08.708
-No. I figure people are like,
"Natasha Lyonne is so New York

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
that because of
her New Yorkness,

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
she probably doesn't want
a stranger to come up

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:12.612 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and ask for a selfie."

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:15.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Eh, it'd be nice
once in a while.

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:17.884 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Will you?

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.419 line:92%
A little, "Hey, nice job,"

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
give me 5 bucks, whatever.

